# ==========================================================================
# Spec Kit
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spec Kit produces three kinds of files:
#   1. Project-level methodology (committed):
#        .specify/memory/         (constitution, the source of truth)
#        .specify/templates/      (plan/spec/tasks templates this project pinned)
#        .specify/scripts/        (helper bash scripts)
#        .specify/workflows/      (workflow definitions)
#        .specify/integrations/   (per-agent manifest)
#        .specify/integration.json
#        .specify/init-options.json
#        .specify/feature.json    (REQUIRED: setup-tasks/setup-plan resolve the active feature dir from this file)
#        specs/<NNN>-<slug>/      (feature-specific spec/plan/tasks/etc.)
#        .cursor/skills/speckit-* (slash commands; agent-specific but useful for collaborators using the same agent)
#        .cursor/rules/specify-rules.mdc (auto-generated; points at the active plan)
#   2. User-local Cursor state (intentionally NOT versioned):
#        .cursor/mcp.json         (per-user MCP config — may contain secrets/tokens)
#   3. Runtime caches (NOT versioned):
#        .specify/cache/
.specify/cache/
.cursor/mcp.json

# eBPF / demo runtime artifacts produced during the talk (never want these committed)
hubble-flows-*.txt
*.pcap
